<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%- include('partials/sprite') %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<% const L = locals.legal || {}; const recyclers = L.recyclers || []; %>
<main id="top" tabindex="-1">

  <section class="section page-top">
    <div class="container legal-page">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Terms of Use and Pickup Terms</h1>
<% if (locals.lang === 'hi') { %><p class="translation-note">This Hindi translation is for your convenience. If it differs from the English version, the English version applies.</p><% } %>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 22 November 2026</p>

      <p>These terms apply when you use our website <strong><%= siteHost %></strong> or app, or sell scrap to Scrap Express<% if (L.entityName) { %> (<%= L.entityName %>)<% } %>. Please read them with our <a href="/rules">Pickup Rules</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      <p>When you send a request, you tick a box to agree to these terms. We save the date, time and version of the terms you agreed to.</p>

      <h2>1. Who can sell to us</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You must be <strong>18 or older</strong>. Our service is not meant for children.</li>
        <li>You must own the scrap, or be authorised by your business or its owner to sell it.</li>
        <li>We buy in bulk from businesses and institutions: at least <%= minPickupKg %> kg per pickup, from sites within <%= serviceKm %> km of Delhi.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="not-accepted">2. Items we don't accept</h2>
      <p>We never buy the following, whoever offers them. Our team will refuse them at the site, and we may report suspected stolen or public property to the police.</p>
      <%- include('partials/not-accepted') %>

      <h2>3. E-waste, batteries and plastic</h2>
      <% if (recyclers.length) { %>
        <p>We hand e-waste, batteries and plastic waste only to recyclers registered with the pollution control board. See our <a href="/recycling-partners">Recycling Partners</a>.</p>
      <% } else { %>
        <p>E-waste and batteries are handled as the e-waste and battery waste rules require. Ask us which recycler your material will go to before you accept a quote.</p>
      <% } %>

      <h2>4. Rates and quotes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The rates on our <a href="/rates">Rate Card</a> are indicative and show the date they were last changed. Your actual rate is in the quote for your lot.</li>
        <li>A quote is valid for the period written on it, or 7 days if no period is written.</li>
        <li>Once you accept a quote, we pay the accepted rate. We only change it if the scrap is clearly different from what you described (a different material, grade or much smaller quantity). Then we explain why before loading, and you may cancel with no charge.</li>
        <li>Any charge or deduction is written in your quote before you accept it. We never add a charge later.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Weighing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Scrap is weighed on a weighbridge or on a scale verified and stamped under the Legal Metrology Act. <% if (L.certificate) { %>See our scale's <a href="/legal#scale">stamping certificate</a>.<% } %></li>
        <li>You or your representative may watch the weighing.</li>
        <li>Our team photographs the weighing machine at your site. You see the photo, the weight of each material and the amount on your quote page.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Payment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We pay by cash or UPI at the site, or by bank transfer, whichever you choose. For UPI, the transaction ID is shown on your receipt. We never ask you to pay us to sell your scrap.</li>
        <% if (L.bankDays) { %>
          <li>Bank transfers are made within <%= L.bankDays %> working days of the pickup.</li>
        <% } else { %>
          <li>For a bank transfer, we tell you the payment date when you choose it.</li>
        <% } %>
        <li>You get a receipt with every payment. A GST invoice, or a self-invoice where the law requires one, is given as applicable.</li>
        <li>If the law requires us to deduct tax at source, we deduct it and give you the certificate.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Our staff and the handover code</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your quote page shows the name of the team member coming for your pickup.</li>
        <li>It also shows a 4-digit handover code. Give the code only to that team member, at your site, before loading. Never share it on the phone.</li>
        <li>If someone without the code, or with a different name, comes to collect, don't hand over the scrap and call us.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Cancelling</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You can cancel a pickup from your quote page or by calling us, any time before loading. There is no cancellation charge.</li>
        <li>We may cancel a pickup if the scrap includes items we don't accept, the site is unsafe, or the details given were false. We tell you why.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>9. Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Give true details and photos of your scrap and site.</li>
        <li>Make sure our team can reach and load the scrap safely, as agreed in the quote.</li>
        <li>Don't use the website or app for anything unlawful, or try to break into it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>10. Our promises</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No hidden charges, and no changing the agreed rate after you accept (except as in section 4).</li>
        <li>No pre-ticked boxes: marketing messages are only sent if you choose them, and you can stop them any time.</li>
        <li>No fake urgency or fake reviews. Reviews on our site come only from real customers, with their permission.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Liability</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We take reasonable care of your site and scrap during the pickup. If our team damages your property, tell us as soon as possible and we will put right or pay for the damage we caused.</li>
        <li>We are not responsible for indirect losses, such as lost business. Our total liability for a pickup is limited to the value of that pickup, except where the law does not allow such a limit.</li>
        <li>We are not responsible for delays caused by events outside our control, such as floods, strikes or road closures.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>12. Complaints</h2>
      <p>Tell our <a href="/grievance">Grievance Officer</a>. You get a ticket number at once, and we aim to resolve every complaint within 7 days.</p>

      <h2>13. Law and courts</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India. The courts at Delhi have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute about them.</p>

      <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>If we change these terms, we update the date at the top of this page. A request you already sent stays under the version you agreed to.</p>

      <p>See also: <a href="/legal">Legal Information</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
